thub.com/users/lkts/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lkts/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lkts/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lkts/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Elasticsearch Version\r\n\r\n8.7.0 and above\r\n\r\n### Installed Plugins\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Java Version\r\n\r\n_bundled_\r\n\r\n### OS Version\r\n\r\nAll\r\n\r\n### Problem Description\r\n\r\nDimension fields in time series indices do not support `ignore_above`.\r\nMapping a field setting `time_series_dimension` and `ignore_above` results int the following exception\r\n\r\n```\r\nelasticsearch.BadRequestError: BadRequestError(400, 'mapper_parsing_exception', 'Failed to parse mapping: Field [ignore_above] cannot be set in conjunction with field [time_series_dimension]')\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis behaviour is expected but not documented. We need to update documentation clarifying that using `ignore_above` is not allowed for dimension fields. Note also that with existing limitations on number and size of dimensions for time series indices and usage of synthetic source as the default, setting `ignore_above` is pretty much useless.\r\n\r\n### Steps to Reproduce\r\n\r\nTry to create a time series index whose mappings include a keyword field that uses `time_series_dimension` and `ignore_above`.\r\n\r\n### Logs (if relevant)\r\n\r\n_No response_","closed_by":{"login":"lkts","id":6067981,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNjc5ODE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6067981?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lkts","html_url":"https://github.com/lkts","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lkts/followers","fo